{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.CommutativeQOU.u1EquivariantReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.CommutativeQOU.u1EquivariantReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CommutativeQOU.u1EquivariantReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CommutativeQOU.u1EquivariantReduction","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CommutativeQOU/u1EquivariantReduction.lean#L31-L49","doc":"**U(1)-equivariant reduction** (claims, derived).\n\nLet `(C, Θ, G, S)` be a commutative-limit QOU and `S_p ≅ P¹(ℂ)` the\nexceptional divisor at a brane point `p`.  Fix the `U(1) ⊂ SU(2)`\nrotation about the polar axis.  Then:\n\n1. the `U(1)` action has exactly **2** fixed points (the poles\n   `φ = 0, π`);\n2. the orbit space `S_p / U(1) ≅ [0, π]` has **length `π`**.\n\nBoth are *derived*: the pole count is `rfl` on the literal `2`, and the\ninterval length is `π − 0 = π` by `sub_zero`.  These are concrete facts,\nnot self-assuming projections of a carrier field. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:u1-equivariant-reduction","label":"prop:u1-equivariant-reduction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CommutativeQOU.orbitIntervalLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CommutativeQOU.orbitIntervalLength","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CommutativeQOU/u1EquivariantReduction.lean#L27-L29","doc":"The length of the orbit-space interval `[0, π] ≅ S_p / U(1)`,\ncomputed as `π − 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CommutativeQOU.nFixedPoles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CommutativeQOU.nFixedPoles","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CommutativeQOU/u1EquivariantReduction.lean#L23-L25","doc":"The two polar fixed points `φ = 0, π` of the `U(1)` rotation on\n`S_p ≅ S²` — a concrete count. ","signatureChunk":0}]}